{"qid":"Q228","names":["Principality of Andorra"],"title":"Principality of Andorra","endonym":{"native":"Andorra","lang":"ca"},"capsule":"Andorra is a co-principality in the eastern Pyrenees jointly governed since the paréage of 1278 by the Bishop of Urgell and the Count of Foix—a role inherited by the Kings of France and then the French Republic. After 1815 the Napoleonic interruption was reversed by imperial decree (1814), restoring the traditional diarchy. The principality modernised gradually, establishing its first separation of powers in 1982 and adopting its first written constitution on 14 March 1993, when 74.2% of voters approved it; that year Andorra also joined the United Nations and the Council of Europe, ending centuries of international isolation.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Andorra's territory of 468 km² is precisely delimited by modern surveys and treaty; its boundaries have been stable since the medieval paréage and are not disputed.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Andorra","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andorra"},{"label":"Britannica: Andorra","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Andorra"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Paréage of Andorra","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paréage_of_Andorra"}],"britannica":"place/Andorra","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Andorra","rulers":[{"qid":"Q7750","name":"Louis XVIII of France","start":1814,"end":1815,"image":"Gérard - Louis XVIII of France in Coronation Robes.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/G%C3%A9rard%20-%20Louis%20XVIII%20of%20France%20in%20Coronation%20Robes.jpg?width=320","imageLicense"